
# Angular Features — Practice Project

A hands-on Angular practice project covering the core data binding features of the framework. Built during INF 354 Practical 4 at the University of Pretoria.

## What It Covers

| Feature | What Was Practiced |
|---------|-------------------|
| Interpolation binding `{{ }}` | Displaying component variables (string, number) and object properties in the template |
| Property binding `[ ]` | Dynamically binding an image `src` to a variable from the component |
| Event binding `( )` | Triggering a TypeScript function on button click |
| Structural directive `*ngIf` | Conditionally rendering output based on a computed value |
| Two-way binding `[(ngModel)]` | Synchronising an input field with a component property in real time |
| Pipes | Formatting output — `uppercase`, `date:'fullDate'`, `currency:'ZAR'` |

## Tech Stack

- Angular (standalone components)
- TypeScript
- HTML / CSS

## How to Run

**Prerequisites:** Node.js, Angular CLI (`npm install -g @angular/cli`)

```bash
cd AFeatures
npm install
ng serve --open
```

The app opens at `http://localhost:4200`

## Key Concepts Demonstrated

**Interpolation** — renders component data directly in the HTML:
```html
<p>Module Name: {{ subjectCode }}</p>
<p>Brand: {{ car.carBrand }}</p>
```

**Property binding** — binds a component value to an HTML attribute:
```html
<img [src]="car.CarImage" alt="car">
```

**Event binding** — calls a component method on user interaction:
```html
<button (click)="Calculatediscount(0.5)">Calculate Discount</button>
```

**Two-way binding** — keeps the view and component in sync:
```html
<input type="text" [(ngModel)]="car.carBrand">
```

**Pipes** — format output without changing the underlying data:
```html
<p>{{ car.carBrand | uppercase }}</p>
<p>{{ car.productionYear | date:'fullDate' }}</p>
<p>{{ car.carPrice | currency:'ZAR' }}</p>
```

## What I Learned

- How Angular's one-way and two-way data binding mechanisms work
- The difference between interpolation, property binding, and event binding
- How to use `*ngIf` for conditional rendering
- How pipes format data in the template without mutating the original value
- Why `FormsModule` must be imported to use `ngModel`
